      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bd0a381e21fa235abe41330|full_name}: 13gb is a ton of memory being used. Most PCs still have 16gb of ram. On my old 16gb ram pc VRC would become usntable at ~10gb used and I'd crash eventually running out of memory. With 32gb it isn't ever crashing but the game has noticeable issues loading new content as ram usage goes up.\nAgain though, most people are running with 16gb of ram, not 32. 13gb is huge no matter what you're using.\n\nThe simplest solution is to just restart your game though. I don't go above 10gb unless I am world hopping/avatar checking or play for long periods of time without a restart.\n\nedit: steam hardware survey shows about 1/3 of people use 8gb ram, 1/3 use 16gb, and under 6% use over 16gb of ram. It's more than likely a VR user has 16gb of ram unless they are running a truly powerful gaming PC for more than VR.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
